 of access to data in a database that is shared over a network. When you open a database in exclusive mode, you prevent others from opening the database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="52156">exclusive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615491">жеке иелік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13773_144171_615518"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A replica that exchanges data with its hub or a global replica, but not with other replicas in the replica set.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144171">local replica</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615518">төңірек репликасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13776_5615_625975"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A supplemental program that can extend the capabilities of an application program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="5615">add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="625975">қондырма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSe