"partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17477_648476_720005"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mailbox used only for collecting journal reports in an Exchange Server organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648476">journaling mailbox</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720005">жұрнал пошта жәшігі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17478_648477_720006"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The folder where junk email is delivered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648477">junk e-mail folder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720006">"Қалаусыз пошта" қалтасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17480_648479_1778378"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Exchange Server 2007, a node in the Console pane of the Exchange Management Console that administrators use to configure administrative access roles for users or groups.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648479">Organization Configuration node</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778378">Ұйым конфигурация түйіні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17482_648543_720008"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email message that is automatically sent by Microsoft Exchange to the owners of a mailbox or a public folder when a size limit, which is called a storage quota, for the mailbox or public folder has been exceeded or is at risk of being exceeded.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648543">quota message</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720008">квота хабары</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17483_648544_720009"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An administrator-defined list of recipients for which mail coming in from the Internet should never be accepted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648544">Recipient Block list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720009">Алушыларды құрсаулау тізімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17484_648545_720010"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An advanced speech codec that is designed for real-time two-way Voice over IP (VoIP) applications such as gaming, audio conferencing, and wireless applications over IP. RTAudio is the preferred Microsoft audio codec and is the default codec for Microsoft Unified Communications platforms.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648545">RTAudio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720010">RTAudio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17485_648546_1778383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Exchange Server 2007, a node in the Console pane of the Exchange Management Console that enables administrators to view a list of all the servers in their Exchange organization and perform server role-specific tasks. The Server Configuration node contains the following sub-nodes: Mailbox, Client Access, Hub Transport, and Unified Messaging.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648546">Server Configuration node</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778383">Сервер конфигурация түйіні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17486_648547_720012"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The level at which the content filter feature in Exchange Server takes a specific action on a specific message, such as rejecting a message or deleting a message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648547">spam confidence level threshold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720012">Қалаусыз пошта ықтималдығы шектік мәні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17487_648549_720013"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A short audio recording, installed on the Exchange Unified Messaging server, that is played to callers by the server. System prompts may be used to welcome callers, to inform them of their options when they use the system, and to make them aware of important information and of events and errors that have occurred.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648549">system prompt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720013">жүйелік хабарлау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17488_648550_720014"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An environment that corresponds as closely as possible to the production environment and within which system and user acceptance tests can be carried out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648550">test environment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720014">тексеру ортасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17489_648551_1490421"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Authentication by using the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648551">TLS authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1490421">TLS түпнұсқалық растамасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17490_648552_720016"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The component of Speech Engine Services that processes text input and produces speech output by synthesizing words and phrases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648552">TTS engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720016">мәтінді сөзге түрлендіруші</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17490_648552_720017"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The component of Speech Engine Services that processes text input and produces speech output by synthesizing words and phrases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648552">TTS engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720017">TTS түрлендірушісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17490_648553_720016"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The component of Speech Engine Services that processes text input and produces speech output by synthesizing words and phrases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648553">text-to-speech engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720016">мәтінді сөзге түрлендіруші</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17490_648553_720017"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The component of Speech Engine Services that processes text input and produces speech output by synthesizing words and phrases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648553">text-to-speech engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720017">TTS түрлендірушісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17491_648554_720018"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of the languages in which Microsoft Exchange Server 2007 Unified Messaging (UM) functionality is supported by the availability of UM language packs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648554">Unified Messaging language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720018">Бірегей хабар алмасу жүйесінің тілі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17492_648555_720019"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Exchange Server 2007, the type of connector that is determined by the intended use of the connector. The usage type determines the default settings for the connector. This includes the SIDs that are authenticated, the permissions that are assigned to those SIDs, and the authentication mechanism.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648555">usage type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720019">қолданыс түрі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17494_648557_720020"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Exchange 2007, the bottom middle pane of the Exchange Management Console. The work pane provides detailed information about the specified Exchange server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648557">work pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="720020">жұмыс аумағы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17495_1266973_2101649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer-aided design file format originally developed by Autodesk; for use with the AutoCAD program to facilitate transfer of graphics files between different applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1266973">Drawing Interchange Format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101649">DXF пішімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17495_648610_2101649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer-aided design file format originally developed by Autodesk; for use with the AutoCAD program to facilitate transfer of graphics files between different applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648610">Drawing Exchange Format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101649">DXF пішімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17495_648611_2101649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer-aided design file format originally developed by Autodesk; for use with the AutoCAD program to facilitate transfer of graphics files between different applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648611">DXF</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101649">DXF пішімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17496_648612_2101650"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A one-dimensional (1-D) connector shape that changes its path to avoid crossing through two-dimensional (2-D) placeable shapes that lie between the two shapes the connector connects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648612">dynamic connector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101650">динамикалық қосушы сызық</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammat