y for each data point. It displays arbitrary text values like Qtr1, Qtr2, and Qtr3; it cannot display scaled numerical values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650156">category axis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1490386">санат осі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17797_650157_2101701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that is displayed in the category area of PivotChart view. Items in a category field appear as labels on the category axis.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650157">category field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101701">санат өрісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17798_650158_2101702"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The point around which a shape or text block rotates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650158">center of rotation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101702">айналу орталығы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17799_650159_2101703"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The small overlap created where two differently colored objects that are close in luminance abut on a printed page.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650159">centerline trap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101703">осьтік треппинг</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="178_38354_2195959"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A violation that occurs when the restriction criteria are not satisfied.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="38354">constraint violation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2195959">шектеуді бұзу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17800_650160_2101704"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A way to see if a certificate used to sign a message is valid. Outlook can check the status of the certificate from the issuing certification authority's database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650160">certificate revocation checking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101704">сертификат қайтарып алуды тексеру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17801_650161_2101705"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a statechart or activity diagram, an event in which a designated condition becomes true. A ChangeEvent is indicated by the keyword when followed by a Boolean expression in parentheses, for example: when (balance &lt; 0)</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650161">ChangeEvent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101705">Өзгерту оқиғасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17802_650162_2101706"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Code that enforces constraints on a table or column.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650162">check clause</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101706">тексеру сөйлемшесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17803_650163_2101707"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A constraint that allows for business rules that span multiple tables. For example, the Order table could have a CHECK constraint that would prevent orders for a customer from exceeding a credit limit defined for the customer in the Customer table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650163">CHECK constraint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101707">CHECK шектеуі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17804_650164_2101708"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control that is used to present a set of mutually exclusive choices. By default, a choice group contains two choice sections, one of which appears to the user as the default choice in the form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650164">choice group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101708">таңдау тобы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17806_650166_2101709"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The point at which transitions split into multiple, mutually exclusive branches, each terminating at a different destination state. One of the branches must be a default branch.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650166">choicepoint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101709">таңдау нүктесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17807_650167_2101710"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small overlap that decreases the knockout of the lower of two differently colored, abutting objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650167">choke</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101710">тарылту арқылы треппинг жасау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17808_650168_2101711"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A superclass that includes class, data type, and interface subclasses. Because all classifier subclasses share the same syntax, they are all represented by the same rectangle model element.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650168">classifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101711">классификатор</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17809_650169_2101712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of collaboration role that is a slot for an object in a collaboration. It is represented by the class rectangle symbol with only the name compartment showing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650169">ClassifierRole</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101712">классификатор рөлі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17810_650170_2101713"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The format that you define for a work breakdown structure [WBS] code or a custom outline code. The mask specifies the sequence and number of letters or numbers required for each level and the symbol separating the levels.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650170">code mask</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101713">код маскасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17811_650171_2101714"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Visual Basic for Applications, the window that is used to display, edit, and write module-level and procedure code.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650171">code pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101714">код аумағы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17812_650172_2101715"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of modeling elements that interact within a given context to perform an operation or a use case. The objects in a collaboration are roles describing types of objects rather than representations of the objects themselves.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650172">collaboration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101715">әрекеттестік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17813_650173_2101716"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An interaction diagram that shows, for one system event described by one use case, how a group of objects collaborate with one another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650173">collaboration diagram</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101716">әрекеттістік диаграммасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17814_650174_2101717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyword or phrase with an associated color that helps you keep track of items, such as messages, contacts, and appointments. You can use color categories to easily find, sort, filter, or group items.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650174">color category</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101717">түс категориясы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17815_650175_2101718"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The part of PivotTable view that contains column fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650175">column area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101718">баған аумағы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17816_1507691_1250221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A supplemental program with the filename extension .dll or .exe that extends the capabilities of a program by adding custom commands and specialized features.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507691">Component Object Model add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250221">COM қондырмасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17816_650176_1250221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A supplemental program with the filename extension .dll or .exe that extends the capabilities of a program by adding custom commands and specialized features.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650176">COM add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250221">COM қондырмасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17817_650177_1161724"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view containing two views. The bottom pane view shows detailed information about the tasks or resources in the top pane view. For example, the Gantt Chart view could be in the top pane and the Task Form view in the bottom pane.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650177">combination view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1161724">құрама көрініс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17818_650178_2101719"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A resource that is formally allocated to any task assignments they have within a project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650178">committed resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101719">белгіленген ресурс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17819_650179_2101720"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a statechart or activity diagram, a relationship between multiple source and/or target states or action states.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650179">complex transition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101720">күрделі өту</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_130364_2001532"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130364">visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2001532">көрнекілендіру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_130364_2398806"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130364">visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2398806">көрнекі элемент</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_130364_2630855"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130364">visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630855">деректерді визуализациялау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2396693_2001532"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396693">visual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2001532">көрнекілендіру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2396693_2398806"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396693">visual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2398806">көрнекі элемент</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2396693_2630855"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396693">visual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630855">деректерді визуализациялау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2626823_2001532"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626823">data visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2001532">көрнекілендіру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2626823_2398806"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626823">data visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2398806">көрнекі элемент</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2626823_2630855"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626823">data visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630855">деректерді визуализациялау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17820_650180_2101721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An implementation diagram that shows the structure of the code itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650180">component diagram</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101721">компоненттер диаграммасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17821_650181_2101722"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A high-level object made of tightly bound parts. A composite object is an instance of a composite class, which implies the composition aggregation between the class and its parts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650181">composite object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101722">құрама нысан</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17822_650182_2101723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a statechart diagram, a state that has been decomposed into concurrent (representing and relationships) or mutually exclusive (representing or relationships) substates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650182">composite state</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101723">құрама күй</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17823_650183_1250222"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A format, such as cell shading or font color, that Excel automatically applies to cells if a specified condition is true.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650183">conditional format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250222">шартты пішім</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17826_650186_1250223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The type of Web Part connection. For example, the Provide Row To connection type passes a row of data from one Web Part to another Web Part.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650186">connection type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250223">қосылым түрі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17827_650187_2101724"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of an individual contact that contains all the information stored in the contact.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650187">contact form</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101724">контакт пішіні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17828_650188_1250224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of buttons used to move through contact items displayed in Address Cards or Detailed Address Cards view. The Contact index moves the focus to the first contact whose name begins with the selected character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650188">Contact index</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250224">контакт индексі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17829_650189_2101725"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft SQL Server or WMSDE database that contains the content for one or more SharePoint sites.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650189">content database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101725">контент дерекқоры</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17830_650190_2101726"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A note at the beginning or end of a text box indicating that the text is continued from or continues on a different page.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650190">Continued notice</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101726">жалғастыру туралы хабарландыру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17831_650191_2101727"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The shape of how scheduled work for an assignment is distributed across time. Use a contour to control how Project schedules the work of a resource.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650191">contour</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101727">контур</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17832_650192_2101728"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The completion of the contract [such as fixed price or lump sum, cost reimbursable, unit price contracts]. Closeout includes resolving all outstanding issues and items, such as inspections or invoices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650192">contract closeout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101728">келісімді тоқтату</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17834_650194_2101729"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of information about a resource's rates, including the standard rate, overtime rate, any per-use cost, and the date when the pay rate takes effect. You can establish up to five different cost rate tables for each resource.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650194">cost rate table</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101729">құн кестесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17835_650195_2101730"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A resource that doesn't depend on the amount of work on a task or the duration of a task, such as airfare or lodging.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650195">cost resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101730">құн ресурсы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17836_650196_2101731"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A task that must be completed on schedule for the project to finish on time. If a critical task is delayed, the project completion date might also be delayed. A series of critical tasks makes up a project's critical path.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650196">critical task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101731">маңызды тапсырма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17837_650197_2101732"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Printed information about tasks and resources over a specified time period. There are five predefined crosstab reports in Project: Cash Flow, Crosstab, Resource Usage, Task Usage, and Who Does What When.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650197">crosstab report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101732">құрама есеп</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17838_650198_2101733"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A specification language for describing data structures. You can use the Crow's Foot entity and relationship shapes to diagram the structure of databases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650198">Crow's Foot</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101733">Crow's Foot нотациясы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17839_650199_2101734"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A color in the Visio application that is stored with a shape as an RGB or HSL value rather than as an index to the document's color palette. A custom color is saved only with the shape to which it is applied.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650199">custom color</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101734">қосымша түс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1784_80052_2212814"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A number that identifies a SQL Server error message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="80052">message number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2212814">хабар нөмірі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17840_650200_776535"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A form that you customize to better fit your needs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650200">custom form</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="776535">теңшеуші форма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17841_650201_2101735"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An .html file whose content is displayed in a window next to a form. Custom task panes can provide form-specific commands and Help content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650201">custom task pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langS