hicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20803_3193169_779254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process by which multiple authors edit a shared document simultaneously, or collaborate effectively even when they are not online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3193169">coauthoring</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="779254">бірлескен авторлық</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20803_747620_3193209"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process by which multiple authors edit a shared document simultaneously, or collaborate effectively even when they are not online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="747620">co-authoring</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3193209">бірлескен авторлық</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20803_747620_779254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process by which multiple authors edit a shared document simultaneously, or collaborate effectively even when they are not online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="747620">co-authoring</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="779254">бірлескен авторлық</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20804_747621_1273106"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of Groove workspace that is an offline, personal copy of a SharePoint site and is kept in sync with the corresponding SharePoint site providing a convenient way of working with SharePoint content, even when the SharePoint site is not available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="747621">Site Client</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1273106">сайт клиенті</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20805_1043088_1131595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A client-side cache for documents that are stored on Web servers. Documents are seamlessly replicated from this local cache, and uploaded to servers as required, enabling faster and more robust file access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1043088">Office Document Cache</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp>