Note><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26373_1273693_2175620"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method for determining dependencies in observations taken sequentially in time, that also supports multiplicative seasonality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1273693">ARIMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2175620">ARIMA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26373_1273693_2176085"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method for determining dependencies in observations taken sequentially in time, that also supports multiplicative seasonality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1273693">ARIMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2176085">авторегрессиялық біріктірілген жылжымалы орташа мән</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2638_557741_1030718"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An element of workflow logic that specifies the event or task that should be performed by the workflow jobs started by the workflow.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="557741">workflow action</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1030718">іскери ереже әрекеті</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26397_1274229_2194828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A formula that calculates the mean deviation of the daily average price of a commodity from the moving average. A value above 100 indicates that the commodity is overbought, and a value below -100 indicates that the commodity is oversold.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274229">commodity channel index formula</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2194828">тауар арнасының индекс формуласы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26397_2223203_2194828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A formula that calculates the mean deviation of the daily average price of a commodity from the moving average. A value above 100 indicates that the commodity is overbought, and a value below -100 indicates that the commodity is oversold.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2223203">CCI formula</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2194828">тауар арнасының индекс формуласы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26398_1274232_2221197"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To execute the current statement and enter Break mode, stepping into the next procedure whenever a call for another procedure is reached.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274232">step into</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221197">қадамдар бойынша орындау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26399_1274239_2202698"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A financial formula that calculates "envelopes" above and below a moving average using a specified percentage as the shift. The envelopes indicator is used to create signals for buying and selling. You can specify the percentage the formula uses to calculate the envelopes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274239">envelopes formula</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2202698">айналып өтетін сызықтар формуласы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="264_181085_2210156"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a database mirroring session, a failover initiated by the database owner, while the principal server is still running, that transfers service from the principal database to the mirror database while they are in a synchronized state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181085">manual failover</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2210156">басқа ресурсқа қолмен ауыстыру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2640_358370_615556"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A copy of a database that is a member of a replica set and can be synchronized with other replicas in the set.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358370">replica</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615556">реплика</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26403_1274315_1320221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To bring a separate conversation, including all its participants, into the current one.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274315">merge a conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1320221">сөйлесуді біріктіру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26417_1274440_2215296"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ',' character that appears in a format string and specifies how a number will be formatted. Each time this character occurs in the format string, the number to be formatted is divided by a thousand. For example, if the format string "#,," is used to format the number 100 million, the output is 100.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274440">number scaling specifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2215296">санды масштабтау көрсеткіші</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26419_1274444_2221485"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A format used for publishing data on blogs and web sites.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274444">syndication format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221485">синдикация пішімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26420_1274447_2177398"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pointer that is displayed as a bar, that is to which the bar type has been applied.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274447">bar pointer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177398">көрсеткіш сызық</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26432_1274502_2212652"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory management component that allocates memory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274502">memory clerk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2212652">жад клеркі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26433_1274511_2220060"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query with an excessive running time, that can lead to a blocking problem. Runaway queries usually do not use use a query or lock time out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274511">runaway query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2220060">бақыланбайтын сұрау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26434_1274570_1362497"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user action, such as a change to status, social tags, or profiles. Notification of these changes can be sent to other users through an activity feed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274570">activity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1362497">әрекет</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26439_1274575_1320034"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user-specified collection of contacts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274575">contact group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1320034">контактілер тобы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2644_14856_626045"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A performer of a song or other audio recording.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="14856">artist</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626045">орындаушы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26443_1274579_1362518"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The status that indicates a user is not working but is on personal time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274579">Off Work</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1362518">Жұмыста жоқ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26446_1274584_2203091"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To switch processing from a failed component to its backup component.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274584">fail over</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2203091">ақау кезінде ауыстыру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26448_1274586_2198375"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A volume that is not in the DPM storage pool and is specified to store the replica and recovery points for a protection group member.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274586">custom volume</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2198375">реттелетін том</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26449_1274587_2201948"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Data Protection Manager (DPM) Client enables the user to protect and recover their data as per the company protection policy configured by their backup administrator.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274587">DPM Client</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2201948">DPM клиенті</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26450_1274588_2201970"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The command shell, based on Windows PowerShell (Powershell.exe), that makes available the cmdlets that perform functions in Data Protection Manager.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274588">DPM Management Shell</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2201970">DPM басқару консолі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26451_1274589_2201983"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that enables DPM administrators to authorize end users to perform self-service recovery of data by creating and managing DPM roles (grouping of users, objects, and permissions).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274589">DPM Self-Service Recovery Configuration Tool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2201983">DPM деректерін өздігінше қалпына келтіруді реттеу құралы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26451_1274589_2221156"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that enables DPM administrators to authorize end users to perform self-service recovery of data by creating and managing DPM roles (grouping of users, objects, and permissions).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274589">DPM Self-Service Recovery Configuration Tool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221156">SSRCT</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26451_1274590_2201983"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that enables DPM administrators to authorize end users to perform self-service recovery of data by creating and managing DPM roles (grouping of users, objects, and permissions).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274590">SSRCT</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2201983">DPM деректерін өздігінше қалпына келтіруді реттеу құралы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26451_1274590_2221156"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that enables DPM administrators to authorize end users to perform self-service recovery of data by creating and managing DPM roles (grouping of users, objects, and permissions).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274590">SSRCT</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221156">SSRCT</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26452_1274591_2201987"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that is used by end users to recover backups from DPM, without any action required from the DPM administrator.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274591">DPM Self-Service Recovery Tool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2201987">DPM деректерін өздігінше қалпына келтіру құралы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></te