artner agreement brings together common bi-directional message processing properties from specific business profiles of both partners. It is a comprehensive collection of all aspects governing the business transaction between the two trading partners. The trading partner agreement is typically derived from the profiles of each partner, with the ability to customize and override the required settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1380152">trading partner agreement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174619">келісім</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27540_2035526_2174619"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A definitive and binding agreement between two trading partners for transacting messages over a specific business-to-business protocol. A trading partner agreement brings together common bi-directional message processing properties from specific business profiles of both partners. It is a comprehensive collection of all aspects governing the business transaction between the two trading partners. The trading partner agreement is typically derived from the profiles of each partner, with the ability to customize and override the required settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2035526">agreement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2174619">келісім</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27546_1380158_2802447"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A protocol that governs the transport channel used for sending messages back and forth between two partners.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1380158">transport protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2802447">транспорт протоколы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2755_550_626367"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chunk of data that a Web server sends to a browser, which in turn saves it and sends it back when accessing the Web server again.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="550">cookie</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626367">"cookie" файлы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27555_1381690_1587662"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A website or service that a customer can connect to in order to share what they've been doing on other websites, see their friends and their updates from other services in Windows Live, or share their Windows Live activity on other websites.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1381690">service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1587662">қызмет</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27564_1382242_2199962"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A plug-in that processes data for a specific kind of data source. For example, Microsoft OLE DB Provider for DB2.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1382242">data extension</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2199962">деректерді өңдеу модулі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27578_1385957_1488980"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows users to navigate directly to the webpage of the top-ranked search result when a search is performed in the address bar.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1385957">Address Bar Top Result</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1488980">Мекенжай жолағының жоғары нәтижесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27584_1387192_1746717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The return to a customer's account of funds that were used to purchase an item. This may occur as a result of a customer's contacting a bank to dispute a credit-card transaction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1387192">chargeback</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1746717">қайтару төлемі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27587_1387436_2355645"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lists files downloaded from the Internet, shows the location of each downloaded file, and allows the user to pause downloads, open files, and take other actions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1387436">Download Manager</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2355645">Жүктеп алу реттеушісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27588_1387437_1488981"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A client-server program accessed over a network that uses a web browser as the interface for the end user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1387437">web application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1488981">веб-бағдарлама</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27588_1406417_1488981"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A client-server program accessed over a network that uses a web browser as the interface for the end user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1406417">web app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1488981">веб-бағдарлама</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2759_210904_1301552"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability of a resource to produce an amount of output in a specified amount of time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210904">capacity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1301552">мүмкіндік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27591_1387494_2398298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A coordinated event where multiple people, not only testers, use a product, which is usually not yet released, in order to find as many bugs as possible.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1387494">bug bash</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2398298">қателерді түзету</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="27592_2071637_2080733"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To restore a device to its default factory settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071637">reset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2080733">қайта орнату</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2762_134154_626945"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability of a word-processing program or a text-editing program to break lines of text automatically to stay within the page margins or window boundaries of a document without the user having to do so with carriage returns, as is typically necessary on a typewriter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="134154">word wrap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626945">мәтінді тасымалдау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNot