ip type="definition">A type of grouping that removes documents with duplicate or near-duplicate content from search results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1783060">duplicate removal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1859763">көшірмелерді жою</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29133_1783061_1859763"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of grouping that removes documents with duplicate or near-duplicate content from search results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1783061">duplicate trimming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1859763">көшірмелерді жою</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29146_1636440_1674738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A source that returns a set of search results for a given search query. The source can be a search service in the local server farm or another server farm, or another search engine that is compliant with the OpenSearch protocol.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1636440">result source</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1674738">нәтижелер көзі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29149_1506722_2306767"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A container for items that are deleted. Items in this container are visible to users with the appropriate permissions and to site collection administrators.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506722">first-stage Recycle Bin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2306767">бірінші сатылы себет</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2916_83133_2214303"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of memory that can be used by one process to pass information to another process, so that the output of one is the input of the other. The second process can be local (on the same computer as the first) or remote (on a networked computer).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="83133">named pipe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2214303">атаулы арна</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29193_1644672_1674443"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web Part that renders named objects or named items in a workbook, such as tables, charts, slicers or a named range of cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1644672">named item view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1674443">аталған элементтер көрінісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2923_59620_626723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of specifying software behavior by system administrators. Administrators set policies that are used to control how software features behave.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="59620">Group Policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626723">топтық саясат</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2925_558978_2070204"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Internet Information Services (IIS) virtual server and port used for SharePoint Central Administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558978">administration port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070204">әкімшілік порт</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29256_1506853_2306769"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A container for items that have been deleted from a first-stage Recycle Bin. Items in a second-stage Recycle Bin are visible only to site collection administrators.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506853">second-stage Recycle Bin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2306769">екінші сатылы себет</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29257_1506854_1587693"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A symmetric encryption key shared by two entities, such as between a user and the domain controller (DC), with a long lifetime. A password is a common example of a secret key. When used in a context that implies Kerberos only, a principal's secret key.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506854">secret key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1587693">құпия кілт</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2927_184441_1320675"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option in the Options dialog box, on the Accounts tab. When the phone is integrated with Communicator, this option uses the automatic configuration settings for the phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184441">Automatic configuration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1320675">Автоматты түрде баптау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="293_147704_1250008"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reference to data stored in a document from another program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147704">remote reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250008">қашықтан сілтеме</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2930_58202_626690"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category for grouping or describing multimedia or games, such as music categorized as "classical" or "jazz".</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58202">genre</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626690">жанр</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammati