pe="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37773_2157393_2239335"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The behavior property of a Date and Time attribute where the date portion of the value is as specified in the UI and SDK and the time portion of the value is always 12:00 A.M.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157393">Date Only</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2239335">Тек күн</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37774_2157394_2239346"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The behavior property of a Date and Time attribute where field values are displayed with no time zone conversion.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157394">Time-Zone Independent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2239346">Уақыт белдеуіне тәуелсіз</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37779_2157426_2346305"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An image file type in which a very short video is followed by a transition to a still image. The combination of video and still image captures the essence of the moment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157426">living image</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2346305">жанды кескін</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37780_2157427_2177332"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo that illustrates motion by blurring together multiple frames of a short video to create the effect of motion in the still image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157427">motion focus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177332">қимыл кезелімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37781_2157428_2176835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The top level view in File Explorer that shows the user's most frequently used and most recently used files and folders or folders pinned by the user for quick access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157428">Quick access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2176835">Жылдам қатынау</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37782_2157429_2176837"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that provides unending stream of music based not on the user's library, but on an artist or song selected by the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157429">Radio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2176837">Радио</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37784_2157431_2176945"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An interval of time that it takes to complete a circuit in a race or exercise course, which the user can record with a stopwatch.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157431">lap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2176945">айналым</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="37785_2157432_2177377"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The total amount of time up to a given point that the user marks while using the stopwatch. After marking a split, the stopwatch continues running in the background.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2157432">split</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:l