S) in one trust domain to delegate user authentication to an identity provider in another trust domain, while generating a security token for the user, when there is a trust relationship between the two domains.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2304645">federated authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2306763">федеративтік аутентификация</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="39497_2361909_2306763"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An authentication mechanism that allows a security token service (STS) in one trust domain to delegate user authentication to an identity provider in another trust domain, while generating a security token for the user, when there is a trust relationship between the two domains.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2361909">federated sign-on</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2306763">федеративтік аутентификация</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="39498_2304646_2306764"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A background process that cleans up ghost records.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2304646">ghost cleanup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Sin