ves, to transfer information directly through the computer's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the computer's processor so it can perform other tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46146">direct memory access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1249208">жадқа тікелей қатынас</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7384_46146_1250108"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows certain devices, such as hard disks and CD or DVD drives, to transfer information directly through the computer's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the computer's processor so it can perform other tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46146">direct memory access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250108">DMA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7384_46147_1249208"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows certain devices, such as hard disks and CD or DVD drives, to transfer information directly through the computer's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the 