kup of transaction logs that includes all log records not backed up in previous log backups. Log backups are required under the full and bulk-logged recovery models and are unavailable under the simple recovery model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274314">transaction log backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2209791">журналдардың резервтік көшірмесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9194_1274314_2221590"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A backup of transaction logs that includes all log records not backed up in previous log backups. Log backups are required under the full and bulk-logged recovery models and are unavailable under the simple recovery model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1274314">transaction log backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221590">транзакциялар журналдарының резервтік көшірмесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9194_169035_2209791"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A backup of transaction logs that includes all log records not backed up in previous log backups. Log backups are required under the full and bulk-logged recovery models and are unavailable under the simple recovery model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169035">log backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2209791">журналдардың резервтік көшірмесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9194_169035_2221590"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A backup of transaction logs that includes all log records not backed up in previous log backups. Log backups are required under the full and bulk-logged recovery models and are unavailable under the simple recovery model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169035">log backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2221590">транзакциялар журналдарының резервтік көшірмесі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9196_181898_2220620"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that is handled in a way that requires much less disk space than would otherwise be needed. Sparse support allows an application to create very large files without committing disk space for those regions of the file that contain only zeros. For example, you can use sparse support to work with a 42-GB file in which you need to write data only to the first 64 KB (the rest of the file is zeroed).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181898">sparse file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2220620">сиретілген файл</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9201_185833_3013796"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A common menu item that enables the user to select how the contents of the current program are displayed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185833">View</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3013796">Көрініс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9202_234512_615439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hierarchical structure of XML elements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234512">XML tree</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615439">XML тармағы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9204_494727_2786150"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A UI container that docks to a pane, can be part of a panel group, and is represented by a tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="494727">panel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2786150">панель</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9206_85254_2093929"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A space that is used to prevent multiple words from breaking if they fall at the end of a line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85254">nonbreaking space</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2093929">ажырамайтын бос орын</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9219_88069_1250123"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain controller that has been assigned one or more special roles in an Active Directory domain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="88069">operations master</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250123">әрекеттер реттеушісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="922_1177130_626325"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process for removing redundant data from a digital media file or stream to reduce its size or the bandwidth used.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1177130">data compaction</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626325">қысу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="922_37103_626325"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process for removing redundant data from a digital media file or stream to reduce its size or the bandwidth used.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="37103">compression</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626325">қысу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9221_141157_2093930"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fundamental data type that holds double-precision floating-point numbers. It's stored as a 64-bit number ranging in value from approximately -1.797E308 to -4.940E-324 (negative), from 4.94E-324 to 1.797E308 (positive), and 0.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141157">Double data type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2093930">Double деректер түрі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9225_25521_1839144"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to the state of a phone line when it is in use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25521">busy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1839144">бос емес</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9230_178677_638238"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A prediction of future events, such as income, sales, or weather.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="178677">forecast</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="638238">болжам</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9234_86568_2093931"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An opaque data structure that defines a protected entity that is implemented and manipulated by the operating system. For example, the system service that reads a file operates on an open file object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="86568">object type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2093931">нысан түрі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9238_116710_615575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A precompiled collection of SQL statements and optional control-of-flow statements stored under a name and processed as a unit. They are stored in an SQL database and can be run with one call from an application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116710">stored procedure</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615575">сақталған іс рәсімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9239_145825_1250124"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A worksheet view that displays the areas to be printed and the locations of page breaks. The area to be printed is displayed in white, automatic page breaks appear as dashed lines, and manual page breaks appear as solid lines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145825">page break preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250124">беттік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="924_233408_719907"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that connects servers using the same communications protocols so information can be passed from one server to another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="233408">bridgehead server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="719907">сервер-плацдарм</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9241_558509_1250125"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of software functionality designed to solve a specific problem or to provide a new functionality to the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558509">feature</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250125">мүмкіндік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9242_143427_2101445"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that stores hyperlink addresses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143427">hyperlink field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2101445">гиперсілтеме өрісі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9246_178335_2195997"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control flow element that provides package structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="178335">container</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2195997">контейнер</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9247_181339_1145198"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A viewable subset of a model that provides focused, business-specific, or application-specific viewpoints of the model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181339">perspective</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1145198">перспектива</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9248_268851_626431"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Files that are used to help detect harmful or unwanted software and to prevent it from installing or running on your computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="268851">definitions</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626431">анықтамалар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9255_298014_626241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button on the message toolbar that compares the names in the To, Cc, and Bcc boxes against the names in the Address Book and against those contact folders that you've specified as Outlook Address Books.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="298014">Check Names</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="626241">Аттарын тексеру</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9258_380750_1305835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An activity that tracks the delivery of a letter. The activity can contain the electronic copy of the letter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="380750">letter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1305835">хат</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9259_397168_2796206"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A filtering list that is used by the Connection Filter agent in Exchange Server 2007. IP addresses on the IP Block list are considered spam. Messages originating from an IP address that is on the IP Block list are stopped from entering the Exchange organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397168">IP Block list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2796206">Блокталған IP мекенжайларының тізімі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9260_321121_1249220"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user interface element that provides users with a quick and easy way to navigate across a large group of opened Web pages by providing the user with a visual representation of all of the opened thumbnails. Through this visualization, the user can easily spot and select a desired thumbnail.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="321121">Quick Tabs</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1249220">жылдам қойыншалар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9266_374348_615473"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web page, published from Access, that has a connection to a database. In a data access page, you can view, add to, edit, and manipulate the data stored in the database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="374348">data access page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="615473">деректерге қатынау беті</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9268_534984_2203207"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A situation where an instance of SQL Server allocates one Windows thread per SQL scheduler, and then allocates one fiber per worker thread, up to the value set in the max worker threads option.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="534984">fiber mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2203207">талшық режимі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9269_535373_2218564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A native format for fast reading and writing of data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="535373">raw file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kk"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2218564">өңделмеген файл</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KAZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</t